      "reviewed_commit": "6f9d7c1373262c541324a16a358785b33ef116cf",
      "reason": "The exact OSV testcase causally reproduces the WRITE-4 heap overflow in pcre2_compile_32 on i386 at the introduced and last-bad revisions, then returns PCRE2_ERROR_PATTERN_TOO_LARGE after the upstream compiler-overflow fix. PCRE2 10.49 contains that fix; all 8-, 16-, and 32-bit code-unit replays pass at the pinned commit. OSV's e19e76ad fixed boundary is an unrelated pcre2grep analyzer cleanup and is not used as evidence.",
